example.paragraph:
Row reduce the augmented matrix $\begin{bmatrix}
      A & 0
      \end{bmatrix}$ to echelon form:

statement.paragraph:
[T] According to Theorem 12, a linearly independent set $\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{v}_{k}\}$ in ${\mathbb{R}}^{n}$ can be expanded to a basis for ${\mathbb{R}}^{n}$. One way to do this is to create $A = \begin{bmatrix}
      \mathbf{v}_{1} & \ldots & \mathbf{v}_{k} & \mathbf{e}_{\mathbf{1}} & \ldots & \mathbf{e}_{\mathbf{n}}
      \end{bmatrix}$, with $\mathbf{e}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{e}_{\mathbf{n}}$ the columns of the identity matrix; the pivot columns of $A$ form a basis for $\text{ℝ}^{n}$.
